In the context of filtering messages, you can specify exactly which fields are returned for a document when selecting from a database. This allows you to limit the results to only the parts of the document that are needed for your application, which can reduce the size of the response.

To filter messages, you can use a selector to define the criteria for the documents you want to retrieve and specify the fields you want to include in the response. For example, you can use the following JSON structure to filter messages:

```json
{
  "selector": {
    "Actor_name": "Robert De Niro"
  },
  "fields": [
    "Actor_name",
    "Movie_year",
    "_id",
    "_rev"
  ]
}
```

In this example, the query retrieves documents where the `Actor_name` is "Robert De Niro" and only includes the specified fields in the response. This selective retrieval helps in managing the data you receive and can improve performance by reducing the amount of data transferred.

